def add(subject,block,day,title,why,facts,static,analysis,trap,question,src,priority='P1',ap=False,precision='day'):
 J.append(dict(id=f'JAN25-{len(J)+1:03}',subject=subject,block=block,date=f'2025-01-{day:02}',date_precision=precision,title=title,why=why,facts=facts.split('|'),static_link=static,analysis=analysis.split('|'),trap=trap,mains=question,sources=src.split(','),priority=priority,ap=ap,status='Historical source check; later legal/operational status not certified',checked='2026-11-06'))
add('Polity & Governance','05 · Parliament & constitutional practice',31,'Budget Session and President’s Address','The Budget Session opened on 31 January; the President addressed both Houses and the Survey was tabled.',
'The Economic Survey was tabled on 31 January; Budget presentation was scheduled for 1 February.|PRS recorded 27 planned sitting days in two phases, with a recess.|The speech outlined executive policy objectives; its promotional claims need outcome-based scrutiny.',
'Article 87 provides for the special address after a general election and at the first session of each year. This differs from Article 108’s joint sitting to resolve legislative deadlock.',
'Use the Address to identify promises for later audit rather than memorising every claimed achievement.|The recess enables committee scrutiny of ministry demands; accountability depends on adequate time, evidence and follow-up.',
'An address to both Houses is not an Article 108 joint sitting. The 2025–26 Budget belongs to February, not January.',
'How can Parliament strengthen financial scrutiny even when the government has a stable majority?','J-PRS')
add('Polity & Governance','06 · Digital rights & identification',3,'Draft Digital Personal Data Protection Rules 2025','Draft rules sought to operationalise the DPDP Act, 2023; January was a consultation stage.',
'The draft addressed notices, consent, children’s data and breach communication.|PRS records a digital Data Protection Board and annual audit/impact-assessment duties for significant data fiduciaries.|Verifiable parental consent was proposed, subject to specified exceptions.|Comments were invited until 18 February 2025.',
'A data principal is the individual concerned; a data fiduciary determines purpose and means of processing. Privacy safeguards should be assessed through necessity, proportionality and remedies.',
'Consent is meaningful only if notices are understandable and withdrawal is usable.|Child-protection checks can themselves collect sensitive identity data; design should minimise that trade-off.|Enforcement capacity and institutional independence affect whether formal rights can actually be exercised.',
'A draft is not final notified law. January’s version does not establish November 2026’s legal position. Do not import GDPR rights unless the Indian text provides them.',
'How can India combine low-friction digital services with meaningful control over personal data?','J-PRS')
add('Polity & Governance','06 · Digital rights & identification',31,'Aadhaar authentication: wider application route','Amendments widened the purposes and entities that could seek authentication permission.',
'Ease of living and better service access were included as purposes.|Non-government entities could submit proposals through the concerned department.|Central authorisation involves UIDAI recommendations, as summarised by PRS.|This was not automatic permission for every business to access Aadhaar data.',
'Authentication verifies identity information; it differs from storing biometrics, collecting a photocopy or determining citizenship.',
'Convenience gains should be paired with transparent, purpose-limited authorisation.|Alternative verification and grievance channels matter when authentication fails because of connectivity, disability or record mismatch.',
'Permission to apply is not blanket authorisation. Aadhaar is not citizenship proof and an authentication framework is not a universal mandate.',
'Evaluate expanded authentication using convenience, privacy, exclusion and accountability as four tests.','J-PRS',ap=True)
add('Polity & Governance','07 · Equality, family law & courts',27,'Uttarakhand Uniform Civil Code: commencement','The state’s UCC commenced on 27 January 2025.',
'The notification brought the Uniform Civil Code, Uttarakhand, 2024 into force.|Coverage includes marriage, divorce, maintenance and succession; reporting also highlights live-in registration.|Scheduled Tribes and specified protected communities are excluded from the reported framework.|This was state implementation, not a nationwide UCC.',
'Article 44 is a Directive Principle, not a directly enforceable Fundamental Right. Reform must also be examined against equality, religious freedom, privacy and legislative competence.',
'Gender-just succession and accessible remedies can be substantive benefits.|Mandatory relationship registration separately raises privacy and proportionality questions.|Uniform legal form alone cannot establish equal outcomes without legal aid and accessible procedures.',
'Do not erase Goa’s historical civil-law framework by claiming no earlier Indian precedent. Verify subsequent amendments and litigation for current-law answers.',
'Can personal-law reform advance gender justice while protecting pluralism and privacy?','J-UCC')
add('Polity & Governance','07 · Equality, family law & courts',29,'PG medical admissions: residence reservation','The Supreme Court examined residence-based reservation in postgraduate medical courses.',
'PRS reports residence-based reservation in PG medical education was held contrary to Article 14.|State-quota seats were to follow NEET merit subject to the ruling’s distinctions.|Reasonable institutional preference was distinguished from residence reservation.|Existing completed admissions were protected, as summarised by PRS.',
'Equality permits reasonable classification with a rational nexus to the objective. Residence, domicile and institutional preference are not interchangeable.',
'National specialist training supports merit and mobility, while local doctor shortages remain a genuine policy concern.|Better infrastructure, service incentives and transparent obligations can address shortages without unjustified residence exclusion.',
'The judgment did not abolish every reservation, every state quota or all institutional preference. Do not generalise the PG holding to all MBBS admissions.',
'How should specialist medical education balance equal access and regional healthcare needs?','J-PRS,J-SC')
add('Polity & Governance','08 · Legislative scrutiny',30,'Waqf Bill: Joint Committee recommendations','January’s event was a committee report on the 2024 Bill, not enactment.',
'The committee recommended prospective removal of waqf-by-user.|It recommended an officer above collector rank for the government-property role described in the Bill.|It recommended retaining a three-member tribunal including a Muslim-law expert.|Parliamentary passage, assent and commencement were later stages.',
'A committee recommends amendments; its report is not binding law. Final enacted text may differ from both the original Bill and committee suggestions.',
'Digital records may improve administration, but disputed ownership needs notice, impartial adjudication and appeal.|The episode illustrates the relationship between administrative reform, property rights, minority institutions and procedural fairness.',
'Do not backdate the later 2025 Act to January or assume every recommendation became law unchanged.',
'Why is committee scrutiny especially important for legislation affecting property and minority institutions?','J-PRS')
add('Polity & Governance','10 · Regulatory administration',17,'Cable operators: online national registration','Cable Television Network Rules amendments changed the local-operator registration route.',
'Registration moved from local head post offices to a ministry-led online process.|Registration permitted operations throughout India, rather than a specified local area.|The fee became ₹5,000 for five years, replacing ₹500 for one year.|Renewal and appeal arrangements were provided.',
'Digitising a licence is not abolishing licensing. Registration reform does not automatically remove obligations imposed by other laws.',
'A unified process can reduce repeated compliance and improve predictability.|Small operators need assisted access, clear transition rules and usable appeals if the reform is to reduce rather than redistribute friction.',
'Compare fee, validity and geographical scope together: a higher upfront fee is not the same as a tenfold annual cost increase.',
'What indicators would show that online licensing genuinely reduced small-business compliance costs?','J-PRS,J-LCO',priority='P2')
add('Polity & Governance','06 · Digital rights & identification',20,'Entity Locker for organisational documents','MeitY described a business-document storage, sharing and verification platform.',
'The National eGovernance Division developed Entity Locker.|Features include government-database integration, consent-based sharing and role-based access.|The release specified 10 GB encrypted storage and digital-signature support.|Examples include vendor checks, corporate filings and MSME lending documents.',
'Digital trust requires authenticity, access control and correction. A document can be authentically signed yet contain outdated substantive information.',
'Reusable verification can lower repeated documentation costs in lending and procurement.|Benefits depend on accurate registries, consent records, audit trails and mechanisms to correct wrong data.',
'An organisational document wallet is not simply a renamed personal identity card. Platform availability does not prove every workflow is interoperable.',
'How can document interoperability improve ease of doing business without weakening data protection?','J-ENTITY',priority='P2',ap=True)
add('Economy','06 · Growth, inflation & statistics',7,'GDP first advance estimate: FY2024–25','January’s NSO release estimated the year before complete data were available.',
'Real GDP growth was estimated at 6.4% for FY2024–25.|The same vintage reported 8.2% for FY2023–24.|PRS reproduced agriculture GVA growth of 3.8%, manufacturing 5.3% and construction 8.6%.|These were constant-2011–12-price growth estimates.',
'GDP at market prices differs from GVA by product taxes less product subsidies. Advance estimates are revised as fuller evidence arrives.',
'The pattern shows uneven sectoral growth; a single aggregate does not describe every livelihood.|Use the contemporary estimate to explain January policy concerns, but the latest official series for a present-day statistical answer.|Deceleration is slower growth, not necessarily output contraction.',
'6.4% is a January estimate, not an immutable final number. Do not silently combine it with later revised or rebased series.',
'Why are advance GDP estimates useful despite revision risk?','J-PRS')
add('Economy','06 · Growth, inflation & statistics',31,'Economic Survey 2024–25: outlook and deregulation','The Survey set the analytical context immediately before the Budget.',
'The Survey projected real FY2025–26 growth of 6.3–6.8%.|It argued for around 8% sustained growth over at least a decade to advance developed-country ambitions.|It highlighted investment, confidence, rural demand and wages.|Deregulation priorities included land, labour, transport and logistics, especially for smaller firms.',
'The Survey is an analytical government document, not spending authorisation or a Finance Act. A forecast range is not a guaranteed outcome.',
'Fixed compliance costs disproportionately burden small firms; predictable risk-based rules can enable scaling.|Smart deregulation removes unnecessary friction while retaining worker, environmental and consumer protections.|AP application: industrial permissions and port-linked logistics need measurable process improvements.',
'Budget tax slabs announced in February are not January Survey provisions.',
'What would smart deregulation mean for a state seeking investment and employment?','J-PRS',ap=True)
add('Economy','06 · Growth, inflation & statistics',14,'Inflation: Q3 FY2024–25 food-price pressure','January releases enabled a review of October–December price trends.',
'PRS computed Q3 CPI inflation at 5.6%, compared with 4.2% in Q2.|Food inflation averaged 9.4% in Q3; WPI averaged 2.3%.|The Survey’s April–December CPI average was 4.9% and food average 8.4%.|These refer to different periods, not contradictory readings of the same indicator.',
'CPI and WPI have different baskets, weights and coverage. Disinflation means slower price increase; deflation means a falling price level.',
'Food supply shocks can persist even when other prices moderate.|Interest rates can influence demand and expectations, while storage, logistics and climate resilience address supply bottlenecks.',
'A quarterly average is not December’s monthly rate. Lower inflation does not mean all prices returned to earlier levels.',
'Why does food inflation need a response beyond interest-rate policy?','J-PRS')
add('Economy','07 · Pay & fiscal management',16,'Eighth Central Pay Commission: approval','Cabinet approved constitution of the next Central Pay Commission.',
'The approval concerned the Eighth Central Pay Commission.|It concerns central-government pay and pension-related review.|PRS linked the timing to the Seventh Commission period approaching its 2026 endpoint.|January did not establish final pay scales or a final fitment factor.',
'A pay commission recommends; the government decides acceptance, financing and effective dates. States may face separate fiscal and political pressures.',
'Pay revision may support consumption and retention but also creates permanent spending commitments.|Evaluate fairness, fiscal cost and service-delivery results rather than only the headline wage increase.',
'Approval to constitute is not implementation. Claims of a confirmed doubled salary or final fitment factor go beyond January evidence.',
'How can public pay reform balance employee welfare and fiscal sustainability?','J-PRS',priority='P2',ap=True)
add('Economy','08 · Financial inclusion & markets',22,'SEBI’s ₹250 small-ticket SIP proposal','The regulator consulted on lower-entry-ticket mutual-fund investment.',
'The proposal envisaged ₹250 periodic investments.|Discounted processing arrangements were contemplated for up to three such plans per investor.|The objective was broader participation among underserved investors.|This was a consultation, not proof of universal product launch.',
'An SIP is a contribution method, not a guaranteed-return asset. Mutual-fund risk depends on the underlying portfolio.',
'Low tickets reduce entry friction but do not substitute for suitability, clear disclosure or grievance access.|Households also need liquid emergency buffers; market-linked investment is not a substitute for every form of safe saving.',
'₹250 is not a government cash benefit or guaranteed monthly return. A proposal is not a final universally applicable rule.',
'What safeguards should accompany efforts to promote market-linked financial inclusion?','J-PRS',priority='P2')
add('Economy','08 · Financial inclusion & markets',20,'Social Stock Exchange: wider-access proposals','SEBI reviewed permissible legal structures and activities for social enterprises.',
'The proposals widened eligible not-for-profit structures.|Suggested activities included disadvantaged-child welfare, vocational skills and scientific research.|PRS records a proposed time limit on registration without fundraising.|The framework remained at consultation stage in January.',
'A Social Stock Exchange provides a regulated fundraising framework. Registration is not automatic proof of independently verified social impact.',
'Formal fundraising can diversify social-sector finance.|Impact reporting, audit quality and beneficiary accountability are needed to prevent mission-washing and unsuitable claims.',
'Not every instrument is an ordinary tradable equity share paying dividends. Do not present consultation changes as already implemented.',
'How can social finance combine wider access to funds with credible outcome measurement?','J-PRS',priority='P2')
add('Economy','03 · Industry & MSMEs',29,'Mutual Credit Guarantee Scheme for MSMEs','A guarantee mechanism aimed at equipment and machinery finance was approved.',
'NCGTC was to provide 60% guarantee cover to eligible lenders.|Eligible loans could be up to ₹100 crore per MSME.|For loans up to ₹50 crore, PRS describes repayment up to eight years and principal moratorium up to two.|The arrangement was time/aggregate-limit bound.',
'A guarantee shares specified lender risk; it is not a borrower grant or automatic sanction. The loan still needs viability appraisal.',
'Risk sharing can overcome collateral constraints and enable productive equipment upgrades.|Due diligence and monitoring are essential to control moral hazard and contingent public liabilities.|For AP clusters, actual access by viable smaller firms matters more than announcement totals.',
'₹100 crore is a loan ceiling and 60% is guarantee cover, not a ₹100 crore cash gift to every MSME.',
'Assess guarantees as a tool for manufacturing-led MSME growth.','J-PRS,J-MSME',ap=True)
add('Economy','05 · External sector',21,'Diamond Imprest Authorisation','A new input-access mechanism sought to support diamond-processing exports.',
'Eligible exporters could import natural cut/polished diamonds below one-quarter carat duty-free.|Export-performance and compliance conditions applied.|The framework required at least 10% value addition.|The announced implementation date was 1 April 2025.',
'Duty-free input authorisation differs from an unrestricted import exemption. Input access can preserve processing competitiveness and jobs.',
'The economic objective is retaining domestic value addition amid volatile global demand.|Traceability, customs scrutiny and export verification are needed to prevent round-tripping and misuse.',
'The announcement was not an immediate general subsidy for every gemstone or all lab-grown diamonds.',
'Why might a domestic processing industry need imported inputs, and how should exemptions be safeguarded?','J-PRS,J-DIA',priority='P2')
add('Economy','09 · Logistics & manufacturing',3,'LEADS 2024: AP a coastal Fast Mover','The sixth LEADS report was released in January despite its 2024 edition name.',
'The pillars were infrastructure, services, operating/regulatory environment and sustainable logistics.|States/UTs were assessed in coastal, landlocked, northeastern and UT groups.|AP and Goa were coastal Fast Movers.|Gujarat, Karnataka, Maharashtra, Odisha and Tamil Nadu were coastal Achievers.',
'LEADS benchmarks subnational logistics; the World Bank’s Logistics Performance Index compares countries. Category labels do not automatically establish an exact national numerical rank.',
'AP’s port advantage depends on dependable road/rail evacuation and competitive last-mile links.|The sustainable-logistics lens adds modal efficiency, emissions and resilient infrastructure to capacity expansion.',
'AP was not a coastal Achiever in this edition. Report year and release year differ.',
'How can AP turn its coastline into lower logistics costs and wider industrial development?','J-LEADS',ap=True)
add('Economy','09 · Logistics & manufacturing',20,'White-goods PLI: third selection round','The round targeted components for ACs and LED lights.',
'The release recorded 24 beneficiaries with ₹3,516 crore investment commitments.|Eighteen new firms committed ₹2,299 crore and six existing beneficiaries an additional ₹1,217 crore.|AC commitments were ₹3,260 crore; LED commitments ₹256 crore.|The aim included domestic component capability and value addition.',
'Production-linked support is conditional. Committed investment, realised investment, commissioned capacity and incentive disbursal are different measures.',
'Component depth can create stronger supplier capability than final assembly alone.|Measure additional output/exports, supplier development, jobs and subsidy cost to assess whether the support changed behaviour.',
'Committed investment is not already spent capital. This round was not the original scheme launch.',
'What distinguishes an effective manufacturing incentive from subsidy for production that would have occurred anyway?','J-PLI',priority='P2',ap=True)
add('Agriculture','03 · Insurance & risk management',1,'Crop insurance continuation and FIAT','PMFBY and RWBCIS were continued through FY2025–26.',
'The overall FY2021–22 to FY2025–26 outlay was ₹69,515.71 crore.|The Fund for Innovation and Technology was ₹824.77 crore.|YES-TECH supports technology-based yield estimation; WINDS supports hyperlocal weather data.|The package supports better assessment and claims administration.',
'PMFBY principally insures yield loss; RWBCIS uses weather triggers as proxies. A farmer’s loss may differ from the index-triggered payout: this is basis risk.',
'Technology can reduce delay only if data and ground validation are reliable.|Tenant documentation, assisted enrolment and timely settlement remain important for AP’s cyclone- and flood-exposed agriculture.|Weather-station density and maintenance affect the quality of index products.',
'The ₹69,515.71 crore figure is not a one-year FY2025–26 allocation. Weather insurance does not directly measure every field’s actual loss.',
'How can crop insurance reduce vulnerability without creating new data and exclusion problems?','J-CROP',ap=True)
add('Agriculture','04 · Inputs & fertilisers',1,'DAP special package extended','Additional DAP support was extended through calendar 2025.',
'The extension covered 1 January–31 December 2025.|The tentative budget requirement was ₹3,850 crore.|The package operated alongside Nutrient Based Subsidy.|Support was linked to actual point-of-sale DAP transactions in the covered period.',
'DAP is a phosphatic fertiliser. P&K nutrient-based support differs from urea’s pricing arrangements; relative prices can affect nutrient balance.',
'Price support shields farmers from external input shocks but may reinforce imbalanced application if relative incentives are distorted.|A durable approach combines affordability, soil testing, reliable supply and efficient use.',
'Calendar-year coverage is not the same as the financial year ending March 2026. Do not assume all fertilisers share identical pricing rules.',
'Assess fertiliser support through affordability, soil health and import dependence.','J-CROP',ap=True)
add('Agriculture','05 · High-value crops & institutions',14,'National Turmeric Board inaugurated','The Board’s launch highlighted value addition and market development.',
'Inauguration took place in New Delhi on 14 January.|Headquarters was designated at Nizamabad, Telangana; Palle Ganga Reddy was first chairperson.|Functions include research, quality standards, logistics, value addition and export promotion.|The release explicitly highlighted production potential in AP and Telangana.',
'An inauguration venue, headquarters and beneficiary geography are separate facts. Commodity coordination must link research, producers and markets.',
'Farmer gains require processing, credible testing, traceability and bargaining power—not only a new institution.|AP producer groups can pursue differentiated products and reliable export quality while avoiding unsubstantiated medicinal claims.',
'The headquarters is not New Delhi or AP merely because those places feature in the event/policy. The Board is not an AP-only institution.',
'How can a commodity board raise farmer incomes rather than merely add an administrative layer?','J-TURMERIC',ap=True)
add('Society & Welfare','03 · Education evidence & learning',28,'ASER 2024: rural learning recovery','The rural household survey measured foundational learning, not only school enrolment.',
'ASER 2024 covered 649,491 children across 605 rural districts, according to reported findings.|Government-school Standard III reading of Standard II text improved from 16.3% in 2022 to 23.4% in 2024.|The all-school Standard III subtraction figure reported was 33.7%.|The report was released on 28 January 2025.',
'ASER is a non-government household survey; UDISE+ is an administrative school-data system. Methods, populations and indicators differ.',
'Recovery is encouraging but the low absolute reading benchmark still signals a major learning deficit.|Teaching at actual learning level, regular low-stakes assessment and teacher support are key policy links.|Use AP-specific tables before asserting an AP rank or precise state result.',
'Government-school-only percentages cannot be substituted for all-school figures. Rural findings do not automatically describe every urban child.',
'Why should learning outcomes be assessed separately from access and school infrastructure?','J-ASER,J-ASER2',ap=True)
add('Society & Welfare','01 · Public health',6,'HMPV: routine surveillance without alarmism','Two Karnataka infant detections prompted public-health clarification.',
'The ministry described the cases as routine respiratory-pathogen surveillance detections.|Neither child had an international travel history in the release.|HMPV was already circulating globally, including India.|The ministry reported no unusual national ILI/SARI surge at that time.',
'Detection is not proof of a novel pathogen, new importation chain or national epidemic. Surveillance findings must be interpreted with denominators and severity.',
'Communication should separate what is known, what is monitored and when advice changes.|Clinical readiness and sentinel surveillance can improve without stigmatising patients or encouraging panic.',
'January’s no-unusual-surge statement is date-specific, not a guarantee for all later months. HMPV did not first originate in India in January.',
'How should agencies communicate infectious-disease findings responsibly?','J-HMPV')
add('Society & Welfare','01 · Public health',31,'GBS cluster in Pune: epidemiological investigation','WHO supported teams responding to suspected and confirmed Guillain-Barré Syndrome cases.',
'WHO described active case search, spot mapping and epidemic-curve analysis.|GBS involves an abnormal immune response affecting peripheral nerves.|Safe water, food hygiene and hand hygiene were emphasised.|Acute treatment can include plasma exchange or IV immunoglobulin, with rehabilitation as needed.',
'An autoimmune syndrome is not a single directly contagious pathogen. A preceding infection can trigger nerve injury; association is not proof of a common cause for every case.',
'Response needs clinical reporting, laboratory support, environmental investigation and critical-care capacity.|Epidemiological methods are more durable exam learning than rapidly changing case totals.',
'Do not call GBS a newly discovered contagious virus or assert an early suspected cause as proven for the entire cluster.',
'What does a rare neurological cluster reveal about urban public-health preparedness?','J-GBS')
add('Science & Technology','04 · Biotechnology & data',9,'GenomeIndia dataset: access and representation','The January event opened research access through Indian data infrastructure.',
'The January headline concerned about 10,000 sequenced Indian genomes and the Indian Biological Data Centre.|A March parliamentary clarification specifies 10,074 healthy individuals from 83 populations sampled at 99 sites.|The objective includes understanding genetic variation and supporting health research.|The later clarification is retained to distinguish populations from sampling sites.',
'A reference dataset is not a diagnosis for every citizen. A genetic association is not necessarily a deterministic cause of disease.',
'An Indian dataset can reduce global under-representation and support better diagnostics.|Managed access, consent, re-identification safeguards and protection against discriminatory use are vital.|Representative evidence and equitable access to resulting therapies determine the public benefit.',
'Do not conflate 99 sites with 99 populations or claim every Indian community is exhaustively covered.',
'How can genomic research support equitable healthcare while protecting sensitive biological information?','J-GENOME,J-GENOME2')
add('Science & Technology','01 · Space',16,'Third Launch Pad at Sriharikota approved','Cabinet approved new adaptable ground infrastructure in AP.',
'The approved cost was ₹3,984.86 crore including associated facilities.|The pad is designed for NGLV, with adaptability for LVM3 semi-cryogenic and scaled configurations.|It provides standby capability for the Second Launch Pad.|The stated establishment target was 48 months.',
'A pad is ground infrastructure, not a launch vehicle. Vehicle development, pad compatibility and mission qualification are separate tasks.',
'Redundancy and adaptability can ease scheduling constraints and support heavier missions.|AP opportunities include precision suppliers and technical skills, but speculative job claims should not be treated as realised outcomes.',
'Approval is not construction completion or operational readiness. Sriharikota is in AP, not Tamil Nadu.',
'Why is adaptable ground infrastructure strategically important to a space programme?','J-TLP',ap=True)
add('Science & Technology','01 · Space',29,'NVS-02: launcher success, spacecraft setback','GSLV-F15 placed NVS-02 into its intended transfer orbit on Sriharikota’s 100th launch.',
'The mission was the 100th launch from Sriharikota and 17th GSLV launch.|ISRO confirmed injection into the intended GTO.|A later ISRO update reported that orbit raising could not proceed because oxidiser-admission valves did not open.|Launcher injection and spacecraft orbit acquisition therefore had different outcomes.',
'NavIC provides positioning, navigation and timing. GTO is not the final operational orbit; successful injection is not complete satellite commissioning.',
'Navigation autonomy needs reliable spacecraft and constellation management as well as launch capability.|Separate launcher success, final orbit, payload commissioning and operational service when reading mission reports.',
'This was not ISRO’s 100th satellite. Do not claim NVS-02 reached its designated operational slot solely from launch success.',
'How can a mission have a successful launch but still suffer a major post-launch failure?','J-NVS',ap=True)
add('Science & Technology','06 · Standards & measurement',27,'Draft Indian Standard Time Rules','Consumer Affairs proposed uniform legal and commercial time references.',
'The draft sought IST as standard reference for official/commercial activity.|Scientific, astronomical and navigation exceptions were addressed.|The associated dissemination effort targeted high-precision synchronisation.|January’s action was a draft consultation.',
'IST is UTC+5:30. Legal time, atomic reference standards, network synchronisation and a local clock display are related but different.',
'Trusted timing supports financial audit trails, telecom, navigation and cyber investigation.|Resilient implementation needs legacy-equipment planning and protection against timing-signal disruption.',
'The proposal did not change the UTC offset or create multiple Indian time zones. A draft is not a final universal obligation.',
'Why is trusted time synchronisation critical digital infrastructure?','J-PRS,J-IST',priority='P2')
add('Security','03 · Policing & transnational crime',7,'BHARATPOL: international police assistance','CBI’s portal sought to streamline agency access to international cooperation.',
'The portal was developed by CBI and launched on 7 January.|It supports information sharing and INTERPOL assistance requests.|Relevant crimes include cybercrime, financial crime, trafficking and organised crime.|It is a domestic coordination platform, not a new international force.',
'CBI acts as India’s National Central Bureau for INTERPOL. A Red Notice is not itself an international arrest warrant; national law governs action.',
'Common workflows can reduce delays between state agencies and national liaison channels.|Faster information exchange must retain data-quality checks and safeguards against abusive or erroneous requests.',
'The portal does not replace extradition treaties, INTERPOL or judicial extradition procedure.',
'Why do transnational crimes require both speed and procedural safeguards?','J-BHARATPOL')
add('Security','01 · Defence & strategy',15,'INS Surat, Nilgiri and Vaghsheer commissioned','A destroyer, frigate and submarine were commissioned together at Mumbai.',
'Surat is the fourth/final P15B guided-missile destroyer.|Nilgiri is the first P17A stealth frigate.|Vaghsheer is the sixth/final P75 Scorpene-class submarine.|The commissioning date was 15 January 2025.',
'Destroyers, frigates and submarines differ in role and operating characteristics. Indigenous construction may coexist with foreign technology cooperation.',
'Fleet renewal demonstrates shipbuilding capability and industrial learning.|Readiness also needs trained crews, sensors, weapons, maintenance and logistics; induction alone is not the complete capability.',
'Vaghsheer is not nuclear-powered. P75 is not P75(I); Nilgiri is not a P15B destroyer.',
'How does naval construction support security and a wider industrial ecosystem?','J-NAVY',ap=True)
add('Security','04 · Defence technology',24,'SANJAY Battlefield Surveillance System','The flag-off concerned integrated sensor information for the Army.',
'SANJAY integrates ground/aerial inputs into a Common Surveillance Picture.|Development involved the Army and Bharat Electronics Limited.|The release states ₹2,402 crore under Buy (Indian).|Induction was planned in phases from March to October 2025.',
'Sensor fusion supports situational awareness; it is not identical to autonomous weapon use or a complete targeting decision.',
'Shared information can improve coordination if communications and data are dependable.|Interoperability, cyber resilience and performance under electronic interference determine operational value.',
'Flag-off is not proof of completed induction in every formation. The system is not a missile or satellite constellation.',
'What conditions make networked battlefield information useful rather than overwhelming?','J-SANJAY')
add('Security','04 · Defence technology',21,'Scramjet: 120-second ground-test milestone','January reporting highlighted sustained combustion for hypersonic propulsion.',
'DRDL demonstrated an actively cooled combustor in a 120-second ground test.|PIB’s April follow-up explicitly confirms the January milestone.|The later subscale test exceeded 1,000 seconds; that belongs to April.|The work supports future hypersonic cruise propulsion.',
'A scramjet is air-breathing with supersonic combustion; rockets carry oxidiser. Ground endurance, flight validation and fielded capability are separate stages.',
'Fuel mixing, stable combustion and thermal management remain difficult technical problems.|Repeatable tests and domestic materials/fuel capability are important beyond one duration headline.',
'Do not turn a combustor ground test into an operational missile flight. The date here is the reporting milestone, not a certified exact test day.',
'Why must strategic technology reporting distinguish laboratory success from deployed capability?','J-SCRAMJET',precision='reporting-day')
add('Environment','05 · Weather, climate & disasters',14,'Mission Mausam and IMD at 150','The launch coincided with IMD’s 150th anniversary.',
'Mission Mausam was launched on 14 January.|The objective was a weather-ready, climate-smart India.|Tools include advanced observations, radars/satellites and high-performance computing.|IMD Vision 2047 was also released.',
'Weather forecasts concern short-term conditions; climate concerns longer-term patterns. Warnings save lives when they reach users in actionable form.',
'For AP, cyclone, rainfall, heat and coastal warnings need district-level communication and drills.|Assess lead time, reliability, user uptake and losses avoided—not only equipment spending.',
'Better prediction does not mean every event can be exactly forecast or prevented. Uncertainty should be communicated.',
'How can stronger weather science translate into fewer deaths in a coastal state?','J-MAUSAM',ap=True)
add('Environment','05 · Weather, climate & disasters',10,'WMO: 2024 was the warmest year','The multi-dataset assessment put one calendar year above the 1.5°C marker.',
'UN/WMO reporting estimated 1.55°C above the pre-industrial baseline.|Six international datasets underpinned the assessment.|Individual dataset values differed.|Warm land/ocean conditions and ocean heat were central concerns.',
'The Paris long-term temperature goal is not evaluated from one calendar-year anomaly alone. Baseline and methodology affect exact figures.',
'A single-year exceedance is an urgent warning, not a reason to abandon mitigation.|Adaptation addresses existing exposure; future emissions reduction shapes longer-run risk.',
'An annual 1.55°C anomaly is not identical to a permanently established long-term Paris threshold breach. Always state the baseline.',
'Why should temperature records strengthen both mitigation and adaptation?','J-WARM')
add('Environment','02 · Wetlands',31,'Four Ramsar additions: January-end tally 89','The announcement preceded World Wetlands Day; newspaper publication followed in February.',
'Additions were Sakkarakottai and Therthangal in Tamil Nadu, Khecheopalri in Sikkim and Udhwa Lake in Jharkhand.|The contemporary total became 89.|Tamil Nadu’s count became 20.|This records the January-end announcement, not a current total.',
'Ramsar recognises Wetlands of International Importance and wise use. It is not automatically national-park status or a prohibition on all livelihoods.',
'Effective conservation needs catchment and seasonal-hydrology management, not only a mapped boundary.|Use the four additions for state–site matching and distinguish this recognition from wetland-city accreditation.',
'89 is not a November 2026 count. A Ramsar site and an accredited wetland city are different categories.',
'Why can a wetland degrade despite international recognition?','J-RAMSAR')
add('Environment','06 · Circular economy & resources',31,'End-of-Life Vehicles Rules 2025','January notification established a vehicle-waste EPR framework.',
'Commencement was scheduled for 1 April 2025.|PRS describes producer, owner, bulk-consumer and registered-scrapping-facility roles.|Producer obligations include prescribed scrapping targets.|The review records an agricultural-vehicle exclusion and differentiated pollution-board enforcement roles.',
'EPR extends responsibility into the post-consumer lifecycle. Authorised dismantling can recover materials while reducing hazardous handling.',
'Traceable records and viable authorised facilities are necessary to prevent activity remaining informal.|Convenient owner access and worker-transition measures complement environmental safeguards.',
'Notification is not commencement. These rules are not a blanket January ban on every vehicle above a particular age.',
'What makes an EPR system credible in practice?','J-PRS',precision='month')
add('Environment','06 · Circular economy & resources',31,'Offshore mineral conservation and development rules','PRS covered operational safeguards in the offshore minerals framework.',
'Exploration/production plans are required for the respective stages.|The Indian Bureau of Mines has a plan-approval role.|Safeguards address sedimentation, untreated waste, marine ecology and archaeological objects.|PRS records a one-nautical-mile restriction from the low-tide line for mining/waste disposal under these rules.',
'Exploration rights, environmental compliance and production permission are distinct. Different coastal/offshore legal boundaries must not be casually interchanged.',
'Resource-security benefits must be weighed against ecological uncertainty and monitoring constraints.|AP coastal relevance does not establish that any particular AP block has received clearance or begun production.',
'The rules have 2024 in their title while appearing in the January review. Do not infer unrestricted offshore mining.',
'How should mineral security be balanced against precaution in marine ecosystems?','J-PRS',priority='P2',ap=True,precision='month')
add('International Relations','02 · Global South & multilateralism',6,'Indonesia joins BRICS as a full member','Brazil’s presidency formally announced the accession.',
'Brazil’s Foreign Ministry announced full membership on 6 January.|Candidacy had been endorsed at Johannesburg in 2023; confirmation followed Indonesia’s electoral transition.|The statement highlighted global-governance reform and Global South cooperation.|Full membership differs from partner-country status.',
'BRICS is a coordination grouping, not a customs union or military alliance. Participation categories carry different implications.',
'Indonesia broadens the grouping’s Asian and maritime footprint.|Expansion offers India reform coalitions but increases diversity of interests and coordination difficulty.',
'Do not call Indonesia merely a partner or memorise a total count without a dated definition of pending/disputed accessions.',
'What opportunities and limitations accompany expansion of an informal global grouping?','J-BRICS')
add('International Relations','03 · Indo-Pacific & bilateral relations',25,'India–Indonesia: Republic Day diplomacy','President Prabowo’s visit connected ceremonial and strategic engagement.',
'Prabowo Subianto was chief guest for the 76th Republic Day.|The talks built on the Comprehensive Strategic Partnership of 2018.|Areas included critical minerals, energy, space, STEM and disaster management.|The statement also noted Prambanan conservation and the India–ASEAN tourism year.',
'Indonesia is an ASEAN member and major maritime state near Indian Ocean–Pacific routes. Cultural ties and strategic cooperation are connected but distinct.',
'Shared interests include maritime stability, resilient supply chains and disaster response.|A balanced answer identifies deliverables rather than assuming a military alliance from diplomatic warmth.',
'Do not confuse Prabowo with Trinidad and Tobago’s President associated with PBD. The 76th Republic Day marked 75 completed years of the republic.',
'Why is Indonesia important to India’s Act East and Indo-Pacific approach?','J-INDONESIA')
add('International Relations','04 · India–US & technology diplomacy',15,'Three Indian entities removed from US Entity List','MEA recorded a specific export-control easing after high-level talks.',
'Removal was recorded for 15 January 2025.|The entities were BARC, IGCAR and IREL.|The list is administered by the US Bureau of Industry and Security.|This did not itself finalise reactors or remove every civil-nuclear cooperation barrier.',
'Export controls, liability, safeguards, finance and commercial contracts are distinct layers. Institutional delisting is not a licence for every technology transfer.',
'The move can support research and energy cooperation.|Benefits still require workable contracts, supply chains and risk allocation beyond strategic declarations.',
'Delisting is not Indian NSG membership or repeal of Indian liability legislation.',
'Why can a diplomatic breakthrough take years to become an operational energy project?','J-USNUCLEAR')
add('International Relations','05 · Climate & health institutions',27,'US Paris withdrawal: notice and effective date','The UN confirmed formal notification after the US executive announcement.',
'The executive decision was announced on 20 January.|The UN received the withdrawal notification on 27 January.|The stated effective date under the notice period was 27 January 2026.|This January action concerned Paris; later separate climate-convention developments need separate verification.',
'Paris operates under the UN climate convention with nationally determined contributions. An executive announcement and depositary notification are different legal events.',
'A major emitter’s reversal can weaken finance, confidence and collective ambition.|Other parties’ duties continue; India can combine domestic transition, diversified partnerships and advocacy on equity.',
'Withdrawal did not become effective on 20 January 2025. January research does not certify the entire November 2026 treaty position.',
'How do major-power reversals affect collective-action regimes?','J-PARIS')
add('International Relations','05 · Climate & health institutions',21,'WHO responds to US intent to withdraw','WHO warned about consequences for shared health cooperation.',
'The statement was issued on 21 January.|WHO highlighted the US founding relationship since 1948.|The event was an announced intention, not proof of completed withdrawal that day.|WHO sought reconsideration and constructive engagement.',
'WHO coordinates international health work; it is not a government directly operating every national health system. Funding, surveillance and technical assistance are distinct functions.',
'Loss of a major contributor can disrupt finance and information-sharing networks.|Institutional reform should improve accountability while preserving cross-border health functions benefiting all countries.',
'January intent is not evidence for the exact legal membership status in November 2026.',
'Why is stable global-health financing a collective-security issue?','J-WHO')
add('International Relations','06 · Neighbourhood & conflict',20,'Indus Waters Treaty: Neutral Expert competence','The legal milestone concerned forum authority, not final project-design merits.',
'The Expert examined seven differences involving Kishenganga and Ratle.|The competence decision was dated 7 January and publicised later that month.|He concluded the issues fell within his remit and would proceed to merits.|India welcomed the result while contesting the parallel arbitration process.',
'Kishenganga is linked to the Jhelum system; Ratle is on the Chenab. Jurisdiction decides whether a forum may hear an issue, not who wins the substantive dispute.',
'Technical treaty disputes combine engineering evidence with legal interpretation.|Present India’s position accurately without claiming every design feature was finally vindicated.',
'The World Bank’s appointment role does not mean it decided merits. Later 2025 treaty developments must not be projected backward or ignored in current answers.',
'Why can forum selection be decisive in a technical river-treaty dispute?','J-IWT')
add('Economy','10 · Employment & skills reports',8,'Future of Jobs Report 2025','WEF assessed employer expectations for labour-market change through 2030.',
'Projected global roles created: 170 million; displaced: 92 million; net gain: 78 million.|The evidence drew on more than 1,000 employers across 22 industries and 55 economies.|Large skill shifts and reskilling needs were highlighted.|Growth includes technology roles as well as frontline, care and education work.',
'An employer-survey projection is not an official census or guarantee. Net job gains can coexist with severe losses in specific occupations.',
'Policy needs portable skills, apprenticeships and transition support rather than assuming gains reach every displaced worker.|AP skilling should be assessed through demand evidence, completion, placement quality and retention.',
'The figures are global projections, not Indian jobs already created. The indexed day follows the dated press text; source metadata differs by a day.',
'Why can aggregate job growth coexist with individual worker insecurity?','J-JOBS',ap=True)
add('International Relations','07 · Reports & global risk',15,'Global Risks Report 2025: horizons differ','WEF distinguished immediate, two-year and ten-year perceived risks.',
'State-based armed conflict led the immediate 2025 risk question.|Misinformation/disinformation led the two-year horizon.|Environmental threats dominated the long term.|The report reflected perceptions of over 900 cross-sector respondents.',
'Perceived risk is not a measured death toll, objective probability or official intelligence forecast. Results depend on respondents and horizon.',
'Interacting geopolitical, information and environmental shocks favour whole-of-government resilience.|Scenario planning and trusted communication are more useful than memorising a context-free ranking.',
'Always name the time horizon before claiming a number-one risk. This is WEF, not a World Bank or UN index.',
'How should policymakers use perception-based risk reports without overinterpreting them?','J-RISKS',priority='P2')
add('Andhra Pradesh','06 · Green industry & infrastructure',8,'Pudimadaka green-hydrogen hub: foundation','The January project package included a large integrated investment proposal.',
'Pudimadaka is near Visakhapatnam in Anakapalli district.|NTPC Green Energy Limited was the named developer.|The announced investment envelope was about ₹1.85 lakh crore, including renewable capacity.|Plans included hydrogen derivatives and exports.',
'Green hydrogen requires low-emissions electricity and credible certification. Project investment envelope, spending, capacity and actual production are distinct.',
'AP has port and renewable advantages, but competitiveness depends on power cost, utilisation, water planning and buyers.|Follow the project through finance, approvals, construction and commissioning rather than treating foundation laying as output.',
'January was not inauguration of an operating hydrogen hub. The envelope is not a direct Union-budget cash grant.',
'Assess AP’s green-hydrogen prospects through resources, markets and environmental safeguards.','J-AP,J-AP2',ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','06 · Green industry & infrastructure',8,'Nakkapalli Bulk Drug Park','Foundation laying highlighted common infrastructure for pharmaceutical inputs.',
'The project is at Nakkapalli in Anakapalli district.|The announcement linked the park to healthcare access and industrial development.|Proximity to the Visakhapatnam–Chennai corridor/Visakhapatnam–Kakinada region was highlighted.|Common-infrastructure costs and hoped-for private investment are separate figures.',
'APIs/bulk drugs are active ingredients; formulations are final dosage products. Common facilities do not remove individual quality and pollution duties.',
'Domestic API capacity can improve supply resilience and jobs.|Effluent treatment, hazardous-waste systems, worker safety and quality assurance are economic essentials, not optional extras.',
'Foundation laying does not establish operating API output. Do not aggregate park cost and investment potential as completed spending.',
'How can AP develop pharmaceutical clusters without creating industrial-pollution hotspots?','J-AP,J-AP2',ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','06 · Green industry & infrastructure',8,'KRIS City and South Coast Railway HQ','Two separate initiatives addressed industrial nodes and railway administration.',
'Krishnapatnam Industrial Area/KRIS City was identified under the Chennai–Bengaluru Industrial Corridor.|The announcement placed it in Tirupati district.|The package included foundation laying for South Coast Railway HQ at Visakhapatnam.|These projects have distinct implementation and financing paths.',
'An industrial corridor is more than one highway. A railway headquarters building is not identical to every railway-zone infrastructure asset.',
'Benefits require coordinated land, utilities, freight links and actual firms.|Planning should connect local suppliers and workers rather than create isolated industrial real estate.',
'Do not put KRIS City under the Visakhapatnam–Chennai corridor simply because both are AP initiatives.',
'How can industrial corridors become productive ecosystems rather than land-development projects?','J-AP,J-AP2',ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','07 · Public enterprises & finances',17,'RINL revival: financial restructuring','CCEA approved ₹11,440 crore for the Visakhapatnam Steel Plant operator.',
'Fresh equity infusion was ₹10,300 crore.|₹1,140 crore working-capital loan was converted into 7% non-cumulative preference capital redeemable after ten years.|RINL was described as a wholly Union-owned CPSE under the Steel Ministry.|Furnace restoration and production milestones were targets, not certified achievements.',
'Equity infusion adds capital; loan conversion changes financing structure. Preference capital is not identical to ordinary equity or cash subsidy.',
'Revival may protect capability and supplier networks, but needs operational reform beyond one infusion.|Evaluate raw-material security, utilisation, product mix, financing costs and sustained cash generation.',
'Not all ₹11,440 crore was fresh cash equity. Approval does not settle every later ownership-policy or production question.',
'When is enterprise revival preferable to repeated support without restructuring?','J-RINL',ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','07 · Public enterprises & finances',24,'Fiscal Health Index 2025: AP rank 17','NITI’s inaugural index placed AP near the bottom of the assessed group.',
'The index covered 18 major states using FY2022–23 data and longer trends.|AP scored 20.9 and ranked 17; Punjab ranked 18.|Odisha led at 67.8, followed by Chhattisgarh and Goa.|Dimensions: expenditure quality, revenue mobilisation, fiscal prudence, debt index and debt sustainability.',
'A composite score depends on indicator selection and normalisation. Publication year is not assessment year; a score is not a legal insolvency finding.',
'AP should examine revenues, committed spending, borrowing cost and productive capital expenditure.|Disaggregate indicators and use later fiscal data to assess change.|Separate measured results from partisan causal attribution.',
'20.9 is not an FY2025–26 score. A zero normalised component does not mean literally zero repayments or zero legal borrowing capacity.',
'Propose fiscally credible AP reforms that protect essential welfare and improve expenditure quality.','J-FHI',ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','08 · Citizen services',30,'Mana Mitra: WhatsApp governance','AP launched an interface intended to reduce routine office visits.',
'The launch offered 161 services in its first phase.|Nara Lokesh launched the initiative in collaboration with Meta.|Examples include payments, revenue/municipal functions, grievances and bookings.|Expansion plans are future targets, not the verified launch count.',
'Digital availability, successful application and completed service delivery are different stages. An interface does not replace legal accountability.',
'Evaluate completion rates, response time, appeals and user satisfaction.|Telugu access, disability accommodation and assisted/offline alternatives are essential.|Privacy, phishing/impersonation and dependence on a private platform need safeguards.',
'161 is launch-stage, not the November 2026 total. An independently unverified world-first slogan is not treated as an exam fact.',
'Design outcome indicators and privacy protections for conversational citizen services.','J-MANA,J-MANA2',ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','09 · Irrigation & disaster resilience',18,'Polavaram: new diaphragm-wall work','The replacement-wall construction milestone was reported in January.',
'Work began on 18 January according to the report.|The stated estimate was ₹990 crore for about 1,400 metres.|The project is on the Godavari.|Panel-wise execution and central technical scrutiny were described.',
'A diaphragm wall is a deep foundation cutoff controlling seepage. It differs from spillway, cofferdam and the full earth-cum-rockfill dam.',
'River works need flood-aware sequencing, geotechnical evidence and independent quality checks.|APPSC analysis should cover benefits alongside rehabilitation, safety, environmental and interstate obligations.',
'Beginning a wall does not mean Polavaram was completed. A political target is not a completion certificate.',
'What institutional safeguards improve complex multipurpose river projects?','J-POLAVARAM',ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','09 · Irrigation & disaster resilience',8,'Tirupati crowd disaster: administrative lessons','Six deaths were reported in the rush for darshan tokens.',
'The incident occurred on 8 January at token-distribution locations in Tirupati.|Tokens related to Vaikunta Dwara/Vaikunta Ekadasi arrangements.|Contemporary reporting recorded six deaths; injury figures varied over time.|This concerned crowd access management, not collapse of a shrine structure.',
'Crowd disasters involve density, flow, bottlenecks and pressure. Blaming panic alone can hide design and administrative failures.',
'Prevention needs timed/distributed access, density limits, separated routes and trained staff.|Incident command needs stop-admission authority, clear information and medical triage.|Systemic accountability should not prejudge individual criminal liability.',
'Do not vaguely relocate a Tirupati token-centre incident to inside the Tirumala temple. Avoid mixing casualty updates from different times.',
'As district collector, design a safety plan for a major religious gathering.','J-TIRUPATI',ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','09 · Irrigation & disaster resilience',19,'NDRF Raising Day and NIDM capacity','Vijayawada hosted the 20th Raising Day and associated infrastructure initiatives.',
'The event was on 19 January.|PIB described about ₹220 crore of inauguration/foundation initiatives.|Facilities included NIDM’s southern campus, NDRF’s 10th Battalion infrastructure and Supaul’s regional response centre.|Supaul is not in AP merely because its initiative featured at Vijayawada.',
'NDRF specialises in response; NIDM focuses on training, research and capacity. Prevention also requires local planning and community capability.',
'AP’s coastal exposure makes training, pre-positioning and drills valuable.|Judge investment through response readiness and coordination rather than ceremony expenditure.',
'Do not conflate NIDM with NDRF or locate every named facility in Vijayawada.',
'How should national specialist response support stronger district preparedness?','J-NDRF',ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','10 · Biodiversity, crafts & culture',18,'Flamingo Festival: Pulicat–Nelapattu landscape','Tirupati district scheduled the event for 18–20 January.',
'Named venues included Nelapattu, Atakanithippa, Sullurupeta, B.V. Palem and Sri City.|The festival ran across a wider bird-habitat landscape.|Pulicat and Nelapattu are distinct ecological locations.|Use current district geography rather than uncritically copying older district labels.',
'Pulicat is a brackish lagoon spanning the AP–Tamil Nadu coastal region; Nelapattu is a distinct bird sanctuary. A festival is not a Ramsar designation.',
'Nature tourism can support local income and conservation if disturbance, waste and habitat pressure are controlled.|Protect water regimes and compatible livelihoods beyond festival days.',
'Do not treat Pulicat and Nelapattu as one water body or every venue as a Ramsar site.',
'How can bird-tourism festivals support conservation rather than damage the resource?','J-FLAMINGO',ap=True)
add('Andhra Pradesh','10 · Biodiversity, crafts & culture',29,'Etikoppaka tableau: third jury prize','AP’s Republic Day presentation received jury recognition.',
'The theme showcased traditional Etikoppaka wooden toys.|The result was announced on 29 January after the 26 January parade.|Reporting highlighted Telugu craft/cultural motifs.|The third prize was a jury-category award.',
'Living craft heritage includes skills, materials and markets. Etikoppaka is associated with lacquered wooden toys.',
'Recognition can help only if followed by fair procurement, design support and durable market links.|Sustainable materials and authentic attribution can preserve skills while allowing innovation.',
'A tableau award is not a new GI registration. Jury results and popular-vote categories are different.',
'What should AP craft policy do beyond publicity to sustain artisan livelihoods?','J-TOYS',priority='P2',ap=True)
add('Culture & History','01 · Diaspora & historical memory',9,'18th Pravasi Bharatiya Divas','The 8–10 January convention connected diaspora engagement and development.',
'The venue was Bhubaneswar, Odisha.|The theme was Diaspora’s Contribution to a Viksit Bharat.|The PM inaugurated on 9 January; the President presented awards on 10 January.|Christine Carla Kangaloo of Trinidad and Tobago was chief guest.',
'9 January recalls Gandhi’s return from South Africa in 1915. OCI status is not Indian citizenship and does not automatically confer voting rights.',
'Engagement includes knowledge networks, investment, culture and crisis assistance—not just remittances.|AP should connect investment outreach with ethical recruitment and protection of vulnerable migrant workers.',
'Do not confuse the PBD chief guest with the Indonesian President attending Republic Day.',
'How can diaspora policy balance economic engagement and migrant protection?','J-PBD',priority='P2',ap=True)
add('Awards & Sports','01 · National honours',25,'Padma Awards 2025: exact categories','The list contained 139 awards, including a duo counted as one.',
'Seven Padma Vibhushan, 19 Padma Bhushan and 113 Padma Shri were approved.|Vibhushan names: D. Nageshwar Reddy, J.S. Khehar, Kumudini Lakhia, L. Subramaniam, M.T. Vasudevan Nair, Osamu Suzuki and Sharda Sinha.|The final three in that list were posthumous.|Announcement and investiture are separate events.',
'Award category, field, state/country attribution and posthumous status should be revised separately. Civilian honours do not confer hereditary privilege.',
'Use the official full list for AP-linked names; Telugu association does not automatically mean official AP attribution.|Prioritise accurate matching and representative contributions rather than replacing policy study with name lists.',
'139 awards need not mean 139 separate individuals because a duo counts once. D. Nageshwar Reddy is listed under Telangana.',
'How are civilian awards distinguished from constitutionally prohibited titles?','J-PADMA',priority='P3',ap=True)
add('Awards & Sports','02 · Sports awards',2,'National Sports Awards 2024 announced','The edition year differs from its January 2025 announcement.',
'Khel Ratna recipients: Gukesh D. (chess), Harmanpreet Singh (hockey), Praveen Kumar (para-athletics), Manu Bhaker (shooting).|Jyothi Yarraji was among Arjuna awardees.|Arjuna Lifetime recipients were Sucha Singh and Murlikant Rajaram Petkar.|Announcement: 2 January; presentation scheduled for 17 January.',
'Khel Ratna, Arjuna and Dronacharya have distinct purposes; Dronacharya recognises coaches.',
'Para-sport recognition supports discussion of inclusive infrastructure and athlete pathways.|For APPSC, revise discipline–award matching without letting celebrity recall displace high-priority analysis.',
'Gukesh did not receive the Dronacharya Award in this list. The 2024 edition was not announced in January 2024.',
'What measures would improve inclusive sports participation for persons with disabilities?','J-AWARDS',priority='P3',ap=True)
add('Awards & Sports','03 · Competitions',28,'38th National Games: Green Games','The Games opened in Dehradun and continued into February.',
'Inauguration was on 28 January.|Host state: Uttarakhand.|Theme: Green Games.|The official account highlighted environmental measures and indigenous sports.',
'Opening date, host, disciplines and final medal table are separate fields. Environmental claims need lifecycle evaluation.',
'A credible legacy includes community use and maintenance, not only venue construction.|Assess travel, energy, materials and waste rather than accepting green branding alone.',
'Do not put February’s final medal table into an as-of-31-January account. Announced green measures are not an independent audit.',
'What would a credible environmental and social legacy plan include?','J-GAMES',priority='P3')
add('Awards & Sports','03 · Competitions',26,'Australian Open 2025: singles champions','The January Grand Slam concluded in Melbourne.',
'Jannik Sinner beat Alexander Zverev in men’s singles.|Madison Keys beat Aryna Sabalenka in women’s singles.|Sinner defended his title; Keys won her first Grand Slam singles title.|Sinner represents Italy and Keys the United States.',
'Revise winner, runner-up, nationality and edition separately. Melbourne is the tournament location.',
'This is lower-priority factual PSC revision rather than a core analytical theme.|Use short spaced-recall drills so results do not consume disproportionate study time.',
'Sabalenka entered as defending champion but did not win the 2025 final.',
'Recall both winner–runner-up pairs without looking.','J-AO',priority='P3')
add('Science & Technology','07 · Scientific administration',13,'V. Narayanan assumes ISRO leadership','ISRO recorded assumption of charge on the afternoon of 13 January.',
'Roles included Secretary, Department of Space; Chairman, Space Commission; and Chairman, ISRO.|He succeeded S. Somanath.|His background includes liquid propulsion and LPSC leadership.|The appointment announcement and assumption-of-charge date are separate facts.',
'ISRO, DoS and the Space Commission have distinct institutional identities even when senior roles are held together.',
'Use primary appointment notices for the operative date.|A dated historical appointment does not automatically certify the incumbent at every later date.',
'The 15 January Bengaluru office visit was not the first assumption-of-charge date.',
'Match the predecessor and three roles associated with the January transition.','J-VN',priority='P3')
add('Security','05 · Extractive hazards & governance',6,'Umrangso mine flooding: rat-hole mining','The Assam disaster exposed persistent safety and enforcement failures.',
'The incident was in Umrangso, Dima Hasao district.|A later state survey reportedly identified 220 rat-hole mines.|A judicial inquiry was ordered.|Rescue/casualty reports changed over time; this note does not claim a final total.',
'Narrow mine workings, flooding, poor ventilation and inaccessible routes can compound risk. Illegal status does not extinguish worker-safety and rescue obligations.',
'Closure orders need enforcement, livelihood alternatives and accountability of commercial beneficiaries.|Mapping, inspection, worker registration and rescue planning should exist before a disaster.',
'This January incident was in Assam, not Meghalaya merely because rat-hole mining is often discussed there.',
'Why does hazardous illegal mining persist despite bans, and what should prevention involve?','J-RATHOLE')
add('Society & Welfare','04 · Higher education regulation',6,'Draft UGC appointment regulations','UGC proposed changes to qualifications and university appointment processes.',
'VC eligibility proposals included senior industry, public-policy and administrative experience of at least ten years with scholarly credentials.|Search committees included nominees of the chancellor, UGC and institution’s apex body as described by PRS.|The draft proposed removing the 10% cap on contractual teachers.|Feedback was invited on the draft.',
'University autonomy, standards and federal relations intersect in higher-education regulation. Appointment eligibility is not the same as a completed appointment.',
'Wider eligibility can introduce experience but needs transparent criteria and academic credibility.|Contract flexibility should be evaluated alongside teaching quality, research independence and job security.',
'January’s draft is not proof that every provision was final law or accepted by all states.',
'How can university appointment systems combine autonomy, accountability and academic excellence?','J-PRS',ap=True)
S.update({
'J-KUMBH':('Indian Express · Maha Kumbh disaster, 29 January','https://indianexpress.com/article/india/mahakumbh-mela-stampede-death-toll-yogi-adityanath-9806048/'),
'J-CHINA':('Onmanorama · India–China talks citing MEA, 27 January','https://www.onmanorama.com/news/india/2025/01/27/india-china-to-resume-direct-flights-manasarovar-yatra.html'),
'J-RGKAR':('SCC Times · Trial-court sentencing analysis, 20 January','https://www.scconline.com/blog/post/2025/01/20/kolkata-court-sentences-sanjay-roy-life-imprisonment-rg-kar-rape-murder-case/'),
'J-USCIT':('Clark Hill · EO14160 history and January 23 injunction; December retrospective','https://www.clarkhill.com/news-events/news/u-s-supreme-court-to-review-the-administrations-birthright-citizenship-order/')})
add('Polity & Governance','07 · Equality, family law & courts',20,'R.G. Kar case: conviction and sentencing','The trial court sentenced Sanjay Roy after the 2024 crime against an on-duty doctor.',
'Conviction was delivered on 18 January; sentence on 20 January.|The Sealdah court imposed imprisonment for the remainder of natural life.|The court declined the death penalty under the rarest-of-rare assessment.|This is a trial-court snapshot; subsequent appeals require separate review.',
'Conviction determines guilt; sentencing determines punishment. Individualised sentencing and appellate review are parts of due process even in cases provoking widespread outrage.',
'Health-worker safety requires access control, safe rest areas, reporting systems and institutional responsibility—not only punishment after a crime.|Assess workplace safety and gender justice alongside evidence-based prosecution and fair procedure.',
'The victim must not be identified. A trial judgment is not proof that every later appeal or institutional-safety issue is resolved.',
'Why should protection of women at work combine institutional prevention, accountability and fair criminal procedure?','J-RGKAR')
add('International Relations','06 · Neighbourhood & conflict',27,'India–China talks: planned people-centric measures','Foreign Secretary Vikram Misri’s Beijing visit yielded proposals for gradual functional engagement.',
'The two sides agreed to resume Kailash Mansarovar Yatra in summer 2025, with modalities to be discussed.|They agreed in principle to resume direct air services, requiring technical negotiations.|An early expert-level meeting on trans-border river cooperation and hydrological data was proposed.|2025 marked 75 years of diplomatic relations.',
'An agreement in principle is not operational implementation. Functional engagement can proceed without resolving all boundary and strategic disputes.',
'People-to-people and river-data measures can reduce friction and support risk management.|A balanced approach distinguishes practical cooperation from unverified claims of complete strategic normalisation.',
'Do not say direct flights restarted on 27 January simply because the principle was agreed. This note does not establish a final border settlement.',
'How can India pursue limited cooperation with a strategically difficult neighbour without obscuring unresolved disputes?','J-CHINA')
add('Security','06 · Mass-gathering safety',29,'Maha Kumbh crowd disaster: governance beyond technology','The Prayagraj tragedy brought attention to safety at very large gatherings.',
'Authorities reported 30 deaths and at least 60 injuries on 29 January.|The incident occurred during the Mauni Amavasya rush near the Sangam.|A three-member judicial inquiry was announced.|The casualty figure here is the contemporary official report, not an independent final audit.',
'Mass-gathering risk depends on density, flow, route design and command decisions. A control-room display or surveillance tool cannot by itself ensure safe on-ground capacity.',
'Cross-read with Tirupati: access points, counterflows and delayed admission controls are recurring administrative concerns.|Independent inquiry should test planning assumptions, command decisions and rescue access rather than attribute all loss to crowd behaviour.|Transparent casualty reporting supports both relief and accountability.',
'Official initial totals and independently established final totals need not be identical. Technology deployment is not evidence that the event was safe.',
'Why must crowd-safety plans combine design capacity, trained personnel and enforceable stop-admission rules?','J-KUMBH',ap=True)
add('International Relations','04 · India–US & technology diplomacy',20,'US birthright citizenship order: constitutional challenge','The new administration sought to narrow citizenship recognition for some US-born children.',
'Executive Order 14160 was issued on 20 January.|It targeted specified children of mothers unlawfully present or lawfully but temporarily present when the father was neither citizen nor permanent resident.|Implementation faced a temporary restraining order on 23 January.|This note records January’s order and injunction, not final merits or later appellate outcomes.',
'Jus soli links citizenship to place of birth; jus sanguinis links it to parentage. The US Fourteenth Amendment and Indian citizenship law have different texts and histories.',
'The issue illustrates limits on executive power and judicial review of constitutional meaning.|For Indian families, actual consequences depend on the operative court orders, not only an executive announcement; individual legal advice is outside this study note.',
'Do not claim January’s order automatically amended the Constitution or immediately removed citizenship from every existing US-born person.',
'Compare constitutional limits on executive action with the legislative authority to define citizenship.','J-USCIT')

